  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5425",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to SW837 through a series of molecular interactions involving the P2X purinoceptor 1 and palmarumycin CP18. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin acts as a target for the compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which in turn targets SW837. This pathway is corroborated by the presence of a similar compound, palmarumycin CP18, which also has a target relationship with SW837. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where doxorubicin indirectly influences SW837 through the activation of P2X purinoceptors, possibly via the action of these compounds. The evidence supports a role for these compounds in modulating SW837, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
